<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:33:50Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Yemen says advancing against Houthis around key Bab al-Mandab strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43c5ea7c1cf8e0f144c944bf7ebcce63abc101726d7e2a915f9c050eb9e78991</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:33:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:45:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-yemen-says-forces-made-advances-against-houthis-around-key-waterway--4e2af6409b56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-yemen-says-forces-made-advances-against-houthis-around-key-waterway" /><summary type="html">Yemen said Saturday that forces were advancing against the Houthis around the Bab al-Mandab strait. This comes a week after the country's Saudi-backed government announced that it was initiating a counter-offensive to take back territory seized by the pro-Iran group during last month's lightning offensive.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Palestinian president Abbas postpones legislative, presidential elections to September 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4ceae9a53ad9fb95c73d9edebc095ed240707cff33853598dd7ca4b1994cfcf</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:33:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T11:56:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-palestinian-president-abbas-postpones-legislative-elections-to-september-2027--79eb133759e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-palestinian-president-abbas-postpones-legislative-elections-to-september-2027" /><summary type="html">⁠⁠Palestinian president ​Mahmoud ​Abbas announced on Saturday that legislative ⁠elections would be postponed from November ​28 to September ​11, 2027, the ​official Palestinian news agency ⁠WAFA reported. In his presidential decree, Abbas set the next presidential elections for that day as well.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Palestinians struggle to find food in Gaza one year after ceasefire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1eadfe06cef7a036d20faf0742010b97945b292eb2a0a6e3b85037ee2bfe954</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:33:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T04:31:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-hunger-and-malnutrition-stalk-gazans-a-year-on-from-ceasefire--12017f60e848.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-hunger-and-malnutrition-stalk-gazans-a-year-on-from-ceasefire" /><summary type="html">Widespread hunger remains persistent in the Gaza Strip despite the ceasefire agreement between Hamas and Israel a year ago that was supposed to allow more food into the Palestinian territory. A new study published on Thursday by Médecins du Monde reported that 93 percent of pregnant or breastfeeding women had symptoms of anaemia, which is closely linked to malnutrition.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>France Protests, Israel's 'politically charged' remembrance, Ethopia, Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb97a0c13b0220c2064bc93ef5fe57d963e9e4f8fec959781cb0d64e2fb8682a</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T18:28:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261009-france-protests-israel-s-politically-charged-remembrance-ethopia-ukraine--45fe531857a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261009-france-protests-israel-s-politically-charged-remembrance-ethopia-ukraine" /><summary type="html">It’s been a week of vigils, protests and political upheaval – from Israel, where three years after the Hamas-led attacks, former hostages and mourners called for accountability over the failures of October 7th, as questions grow over the stalled path to peace in Gaza; to France, where mass demonstrations over chronic underfunding and poor conditions have drawn students, unions and hundreds of thousands of protesters into the streets, just months ahead of a presidential election. In Spain, Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez has made the housing crisis the centrepiece of a high-stakes electoral gamble, as protests intensify following the death of a pensioner whose eviction helped ignite the movement. And in the UK, questions remain over a suspected Iranian plot targeting US aircraft at RAF Fairford, after American B-1 bombers were hastily withdrawn amid warnings of a serious and immediate threat.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>FlyDubai co-pilot planned suicide attack on Tel Aviv airport inspired by 9/11, prosecutor says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98377facfcf29db76fcda40902c7c0c0385eaabb64af88096e84c325b8c27fff</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T17:04:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261009-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-suicide-attack-on-tel-aviv-airport-inspired-by-9-11--e457237ce44f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261009-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-suicide-attack-on-tel-aviv-airport-inspired-by-9-11" /><summary type="html">The Omani co-pilot who attacked the captain of FlyDubai flight 1073 had planned to crash the plane into Tel Aviv's international airport in a suicide attack, the United Arab Emirates' top prosecutor said Friday. The Israel-bound flight carrying 182 people made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a descent so extreme that part of its rudder was torn away.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Palestinians gained 'nothing' from October 7, Egyptian businessman Naguib Sawiris says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7325d9d8073acf03c241e4ae37156faa25c38333b6da310fb396ee261af063cf</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:12:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261008-palestinians-gained-nothing-from-october-7-egyptian-businessman-naguib-sawiris-says--ebd948c43a7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261008-palestinians-gained-nothing-from-october-7-egyptian-businessman-naguib-sawiris-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Egyptian businessman Naguib Sawiris called the October 7 attacks a "horrible act of terrorism" that brought Palestinians "only destruction", while warning of an "expansionist" Israeli government. He also said that the economic fallout from the Iran war is already "happening", defended doubling his UAE investment despite the regional conflict, and praised Syria's new president.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz crisis fuels Cairo's plastic recycling business</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14415af79d6baf03220ffa3db7ce90c28b84dc67cacc41a580c6f7686dbf007f</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T09:44:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261008-strait-of-hormuz-crisis-fuels-cairo-s-plastic-recycling-business--f882feb0c766.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261008-strait-of-hormuz-crisis-fuels-cairo-s-plastic-recycling-business" /><summary type="html">In the heart of the Egyptian capital Cairo, within the labyrinthine streets of the Manshiyet Nasser district, nearly 120,000 residents process a third of the megacity's waste every day. Long marginalised, these informal recycling specialists are now undergoing a dramatic transformation due to geopolitical tensions in the Strait of Hormuz, through which polyethylene from the Gulf usually passes.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Diplomats take shelter in Saudi capital as Yemen's Houthis target Riyadh airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eac428c316a16918f9602e0620c12e23df841104fdc7774611ff5026a32896f0</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T09:20:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261008-diplomats-school-pupils-take-shelter-in-saudi-capital-as-yemen-s-houthis-step-up-attacks--02a4c212cf4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261008-diplomats-school-pupils-take-shelter-in-saudi-capital-as-yemen-s-houthis-step-up-attacks" /><summary type="html">Foreign diplomats and international schools in the Saudi capital took safety measures on Thursday as loud blasts rattled the city and Yemen's Houthi rebels claimed missile attacks against its airport. In a further blow to Riyadh, Turkey ruled out sending troops to confront the Iran-backed militia, despite a defence pact with Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'Most Israeli citizens lost confidence' in govt: Leaders 'shift' blame, 'block' commission inquiry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:314acc17c8e2d6a87cc404b37246d92d704ebc44c54ecdf22e12cfab1d306ec4</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T07:42:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/most-israeli-citizens-lost-confidence-in-govt-pm-leaders-shift-blame-block-commission-inquiry--e43af2e8bbca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/most-israeli-citizens-lost-confidence-in-govt-pm-leaders-shift-blame-block-commission-inquiry" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry welcomes Guy Poran, a former Israeli Air Force officer and member of Mistaclim (Looking the Occupation in the Eye). Poran sees October 7 as a profound rupture in Israeli society following the unprecedented Hamas attack, which targeted civilians across generations. He argues that responsibility for the failures cannot be separated from the policies that preceded the attack, including the Netanyahu government's approach toward Hamas. Without political change, Poran sees little prospect of repairing relations between Israelis and Palestinians or creating the conditions for a lasting peace, which he regards as crucial to Israel's future.</summary></entry><entry><title>Explosions heard in Saudi capital Riyadh after Houthis' deadly attacks on airports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9f295ce4492476dc4af891114b4aadfb6dbf23a78d7d880dd0fed09bd2eaa0e</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T03:02:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261008-saudi-arabia-strikes-deadly-houthi-attacks-airports--3a7a45587e74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261008-saudi-arabia-strikes-deadly-houthi-attacks-airports" /><summary type="html">Several explosions were reported on Thursday in Saudi Arabia’s capital Riyadh amid ongoing fighting between the kingdom and Yemen's Houthis. A day earlier, three people were killed and 36 wounded in attacks on Abha and Riyadh’s King Khalid international airports claimed by the Iran-backed rebel group.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>No longer the same Israel? October 7 and the future of the Jewish State</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5e42fcc8f249541d43769440299f5f204b55ad7179690c5d0896dd6d01b9130</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T22:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261007-no-longer-the-same-israel-october-7th-and-the-future-of-the-jewish-state--0c0ca85a23b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261007-no-longer-the-same-israel-october-7th-and-the-future-of-the-jewish-state" /><summary type="html">For now, it's still Benjamin Netanyahu's Israel. In 2023, in the immediate aftermath of the country's worst day of bloodshed in its history, pundits predicted the quick demise of the right-wing prime minister. But on the third anniversary of the October 7 attacks, Israel's still not reckoned with the security failures on the day, the root causes of the Hamas-led terror attack, the brutal war of vengeance that followed and above all, Netanyahu is still prime minister with a fair shot at re-election. Even if the Likud leader is voted out on October 27, his most serious election rivals don't exactly advocate for a radical break when it comes to the Palestinians.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Israel marks three years since October 7 attacks with strikes on Gaza, political debate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ca682dc339063fd7891e332899cbd5d4fbf63be6fd35f673b722b3024de99da</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T21:50:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-israel-three-years-october-7-attack-elections--31dcc478ed4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-israel-three-years-october-7-attack-elections" /><summary type="html">Israel marked the third anniversary of Hamas’s October 7 attack on Wednesday with gatherings in tribute and renewed strikes on Gaza as political debate intensified ahead of elections. Gaza officials said strikes on the territory had killed five people despite a year-old ceasefire agreement.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'It's still unclear whether Netanyahu will pay for what happened during his time in office'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc82756fc95f2050c9da4060ead6f0b26af8fe5a0b633c255202dafe186af1d3</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T19:52:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/it-s-still-unclear-whether-netanyahu-will-pay-for-what-happened-during-his-time-in-office--eb0eadf0c235.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-s-still-unclear-whether-netanyahu-will-pay-for-what-happened-during-his-time-in-office" /><summary type="html">As Israel marks the third anniversary of the October 7 attacks, questions linger about the warnings Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu received about them. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Ayala Panievsky, Lecturer at City University of London and author of The New Censorship, explains that the allegations in the run-up to the elections "are very damaging for Netanyahu but there are some factors mitigating the risk for him", including a fragmented opposition as well as the control of major media.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Resilience' of Israelis as they mourn the loss of loved ones and 'the sense that we can be safe'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cd0c4da78991f3a86ce620178745b0fe1d64ef8d80bbcc37036c524cdf8a447</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T17:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-resilience-of-israelis-as-they-the-mourn-loss-of-loved-ones-and-the-sense-that-we-can-be-sa--2d3e0a573603.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-resilience-of-israelis-as-they-the-mourn-loss-of-loved-ones-and-the-sense-that-we-can-be-safe" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Dr. Danny Brom, Founding Director of METIV, the Israel Psychotrauma Center in Jerusalem. According to Dr. Brom, as Israelis and Jewish people around the world continue to mourn the largest loss of Jewish life on a single day since the Holocaust, their fundamental sense of collective security has also been shattered. What strikes him, however, is the resilience that exists alongside the grieving. How can individuals, communities and society rebuild a sense of safety without allowing fear to dictate the future? Yet, as Dr. Brom observes, “the war is still going on,” while political leaders speak of pursuing “the ultimate victory, which no one really knows what that is.”</summary></entry><entry><title>October 7: Former Israeli hostage speaks to France 24</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:902aa817527805103196364a19ae45f4342875aacf96bfffc92140111968650e</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:30:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-former-israeli-hostage-speaks-to-france-24--e8ba8788da8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-former-israeli-hostage-speaks-to-france-24" /><summary type="html">“The terrorists pulled us out through the window. They handcuffed me and pushed us into a car that they had brought from Gaza.”
 
Former Israeli hostage Shoshan Haran speaks to France 24.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Time doesn't heal': Parents of October 7 attacks victim Aner Shapira</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a23921d961aaf5516126dac944fef737c873399399df084835d51f1633d55d8a</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T12:59:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261007-time-doesn-t-heal-parents-of-aner-shapira-killed-on-october-7-2023--eab3eadca183.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261007-time-doesn-t-heal-parents-of-aner-shapira-killed-on-october-7-2023" /><summary type="html">The parents of a 22-year-old Israeli man who was killed when Hamas attacked the Nova music festival on October 7, 2023 have told FRANCE 24 how they can still feel him surrounding them even though he's no longer here. Shira and Moshe Shapira say that time doesn't heal, but they are learning how to live with their loss. Their son Aner managed to throw seven grenades back towards Hamas fighters, before an eighth exploded in his hands, killing him. They spoke to us in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>October 7: Israelis mark three years since Hamas attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd4a68f70613d9ad4c25d1381b80ba54528f0bc9b7eafbf9148302501a5e04f6</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T11:04:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-israelis-mark-three-years-since-hamas-attacks--ad8ab7db6b13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-israelis-mark-three-years-since-hamas-attacks" /><summary type="html">Israel is marking the third anniversary of the October 7, 2023, Hamas terrorist attack on Wednesday with memorials across the country.
 
At the site of the Nova music festival, where more than 300 people were killed, families gathered at dawn for a moment of silence and paid tribute in front of portraits both of festival-goers and security forces who died on October 7.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli papers commemorate October 7 attacks, three years on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91b0fd9b292b415e24ea0d8d675dbe1834ec8f671f8d04fe70a200e5aff9ebef</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T10:55:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261007-israeli-papers-commemorate-october-7-attacks-three-years-on--ccedc373b92b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261007-israeli-papers-commemorate-october-7-attacks-three-years-on" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, October 7: Papers mark the third anniversary of the October 7 attacks. But first: the high school protests that have swept across France make the front pages at home and abroad. Also, the Argentinian press waves off Lionel Messi after his last international match. Finally, a British adventurer completes a 28-year walk around the world.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>How Netanyahu survived the political fallout from the October 7 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4aff0b63ae400967e04d7a66160bbe91baa372eb8bf086e23b18a3a5a5098861</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T05:24:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-how-netanyahu-survived-the-political-fallout-from-the-october-7-attacks--7a662194365a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-how-netanyahu-survived-the-political-fallout-from-the-october-7-attacks" /><summary type="html">Three years after the deadly Hamas-led October 7 attacks in southern Israel, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is fighting for political survival ahead of legislative elections later this month. Reports that Arab leaders warned him of the assault in advance have undercut his claims that Israel's security chiefs are to blame, but his political base appears to be holding.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>French FM denounces 'poison' of anti-Semitism as Israel marks October 7 attacks anniversary</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:385f837ede0f32b1f7096e22d0e3eecd8f81698a3d5f6107b5d2a24d87dd4c8b</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:46:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-middle-east-live-houthis-target-airport-in-yemen-as-israel-marks-october-7-anniversary--7d575027777c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-middle-east-live-houthis-target-airport-in-yemen-as-israel-marks-october-7-anniversary" /><summary type="html">Israelis on Wednesday took part in commemorations for the victims of Hamas's October 7, 2023 attacks, which killed 1,200 people and saw 251 hostages taken. French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot denounced the "poison of anti-Semitism" as he attended a memorial ceremony at the site of the Nova music festival massacre. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel marks third anniversary of October 7 attack as election looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d59dfb5e26774f68860735379fb14cd6396968951bbbe0f1b3544cdc750540f1</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:14:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-israel-marks-third-anniversary-of-october-7-attack-as-election-looms--bcd3022d5ccb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-israel-marks-third-anniversary-of-october-7-attack-as-election-looms" /><summary type="html">Israel will mark the third anniversary of the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack on Wednesday with memorial events across the country, as heightened security surrounds the commemorations and voters prepare for an election in which the deadliest day in Israel’s history is expected to remain a central issue.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'We were naive' about Hamas, Israeli ex-hostage Shoshan Haran says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ba8fe299cf6c98477d31df4dc2a04b567bd369a1f0112f30b26f58376a06039</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says--83490e71ebdf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israeli former hostage Shoshan Haran said "we were naive" about Hamas before the October 7, 2023 attack on her kibbutz. Held in Gaza for 50 days, she recalled refusing to "show weakness" to her captors. She also called the accusations of genocide against Israel "a lie" and shared her late husband's last words.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Israel warns Gazans will pay 'heavy price' for any October 7 attacks on military</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78151262b5106560a7561def331a198ab03d52f56366c17f64bc8018f16b7aec</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T07:50:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261006-israel-warns-gazans-will-pay-heavy-price-for-any-october-7-attacks-on-military--16171ff124a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261006-israel-warns-gazans-will-pay-heavy-price-for-any-october-7-attacks-on-military" /><summary type="html">Israel on Tuesday said that Hamas and the Palestinian population in Gaza would pay a "heavy price" if any of Israel's armed forces were harmed on the three-year anniversary of the militant group's October 7 attack.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi-backed Yemeni forces expel the Houthis from several areas around key strait, officials say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e1ec83c99fdc48476d2f1b66a83493b95debe8766024e03e599edd1fe62ac6d</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T19:17:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say--6def5d5b3087.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say" /><summary type="html">Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces staged a lightning advance on ​Monday to retake the coast around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait up to the city of Mocha, the government said, pushing the Iran-backed Houthis out of most of the areas they seized last month. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>ISIS suspects face 'outsourced' justice in Iraq as HRW warns of 'collective global detention crisis'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b6d4e0c95910bea3e261c3a7c6710be036d062590529de5f848ba83b0dab75f</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:46:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-c--177d80f183d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-crisis-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Letta Tayler, Senior Counterterrorism Advisor at Human Rights Watch. She warns of the detention of suspected Islamic State members transferred from northeast Syria to Iraq as part of a much wider "global detention crisis". The men and boys now held in Iraq are living in 'dire' conditions, including deaths from illness, allegations of torture, and serious questions surrounding access to effective legal representation. Can accountability be achieved through legal proceedings that respect the rule of law and provide genuine justice to both detainees and victims?</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis claim attacks on Riyadh airport as Saudi-led forces strike Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbcf76cfd9879bbd7a9829736bf53d33c5ccf9bf0793a3ae1570b08ae41108dc</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T08:12:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261005-yemen-military-announces-broad-range-of-strikes-against-houthis-in-bid-to-retake-lost-terri--eb1150ba341e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261005-yemen-military-announces-broad-range-of-strikes-against-houthis-in-bid-to-retake-lost-territory" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Houthis said Monday they had struck Riyadh's international airport and an Aramco refinery as Saudi-led forces intensified attacks on Houthi positions in Yemen in a bid to retake territory. Pakistan and Turkey also pledged troops to Saudi Arabia under a new defence pact.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran says no military solution to war as peace talks with US stall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b0caf7302dc8b3c0ccef55151fd3dad022a8f2554b225148bd744ad4c1de8de</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T21:41:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks--489f2da42d26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">Iran's diplomat said on Sunday there was no military solution to the US war against Iran as peace talks appeared stalled. Washington has scaled back attacks in favour of economic pressure, while Iran's attempted Hormuz blockade remains contentious. A UK maritime agency reported another tanker hit by an unidentified projectile.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Disaster averted on Flydubai flight, French school protests and Bangkok floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcfae6a72e3052d2e3e2482c7400f159e2a710edadef9ef95d78a2c269907edd</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:35:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-the-week-in-pictures-disaster-averted-flydubai-flight-french-school-protests-and-bangkok-fl--aacc58ef2e53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-the-week-in-pictures-disaster-averted-flydubai-flight-french-school-protests-and-bangkok-floods" /><summary type="html">From French highschoolers protesting to demand better learning conditions to a Flydubai flight diverted to Saudi Arabia after a flightcrew member's onboard attack and flooded streets in Bangkok, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's government declares counter-offensive as Houthis cut vital route to besieged city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9f1a299b7c506328b1857e84a8ea859e45adc7126734e2298bab332a502a452</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz--d567521fb6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz" /><summary type="html">The ​leader of ​Yemen's Saudi-backed government announced the beginning of a ​major ‌military ⁠operation against the Iran-backed Houthis ‌on Sunday aimed at ⁠recapturing territory under their control. The announcement came as Houthi forces cut off a vital supply route to the besieged government-held city of Taiz, according to several security sources.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Palestinians ‘harassed’ by settlers’ increasing use of drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4617e975025bab0e42df7c71ae4fab92d82880fa6e75293c53d11ca84d7a714</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:01:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones--66a927f7344d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones" /><summary type="html">Palestinians and activists report an increased use of drones in the occupied West Bank, particularly by the army and settlers, to whom the government supplies the drones directly. The drones are used to intimidate, monitor, demolish and make daily life unbearable.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
